From 1a0dd7f8c34481264638a6d5edce45819f33782d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:04:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] io_uring/futex: return a wait's data to the cache when it
 fails to arm

io_futex_wait() takes its io_futex_data from ctx->futex_cache, and a
completed wait gives it back (io_futex_complete()).  A wait that fails to
arm instead frees it with io_req_async_data_free(), which is kfree().
The usual failure is -EAGAIN from futex_wait_setup(): the futex word no
longer holds the expected value.  That is routine for a waiter that
re-arms with the value it last read, since the word moves every time
there is something to wake for.  Each such failure takes an object out
of the cache for good, so the cache drains, and from then on the waits
that miss it allocate from kmalloc-192 instead.

Measured on an event loop re-arming one IORING_OP_FUTEX_WAIT per
message under load: 0.39 arms per message failed with -EAGAIN, and the waiter
did 0.39 kmalloc() and kfree() per message.  On PREEMPT_RT a kmalloc()
or kfree() that misses the per-CPU slab takes the node's list_lock, a
sleeping lock shared with every other user of the cache.

Put the data back in the cache on that path, as the completion path
does, while the cache is still under the submit lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GpUwwinTvks4P7qHQAefc5

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 io_uring/futex.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/io_uring/futex.c b/io_uring/futex.c
index 64f3bd51c84c..707305f3536c 100644
--- a/io_uring/futex.c
+++ b/io_uring/futex.c
@@ -301,6 +301,16 @@ int io_futex_wait(struct io_kiocb *req, unsigned int issue_flags)
 		return IOU_ISSUE_SKIP_COMPLETE;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Back to the cache it came from, as io_futex_complete() does, while
+	 * the cache is still ours.  -EAGAIN (the futex word already changed) is
+	 * a routine outcome for a waiter that re-arms with the value it last
+	 * saw; freeing it here would drain the cache, and every later wait
+	 * would allocate.
+	 */
+	io_cache_free(&ctx->futex_cache, ifd);
+	io_req_async_data_clear(req, 0);
+
 done_unlock:
 	io_ring_submit_unlock(ctx, issue_flags);
 done:
